      "contextBefore": "Parameters",
      "contextAfter": "`sigma`: The standard deviation of the gaussian blur filter. Gaussian weight `w`, centered at `0`, at integer grid `i`, is given as: `w(i) = 1/sqrt(2*pi*sigma) * exp(-i^2/2*sigma^2)` If we take cut off at 1% of `w(0)` (max weight) beyond which weights are considered `0`, we have `ceil(sqrt(-log(0.01)*2)*sigma) ~ ceil(3.7*sigma)` as the rough estimate of the filter width.",
